{"c":[{"id":"14ad6d2ac531038b","sum":"Measured 2026-10-21 (pre-drop): DuckDB 2.0.0 vss filters WHERE inside the HNSW scan, 1.5.4 post-filters; pragma_hnsw_index_info approx_memory_usage is in-memory size, not disk bytes. Historical only: stockroom now ranks exactly and keeps no index.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261022T012046Z-e14849db8f091ac7","text":"DuckDB 2.0.0 vss filters a WHERE inside the HNSW scan (EXPLAIN: Filters: optional); it found 1 in-scope row behind 2,048 nearer rows but none behind 4,096 identical ones (4/4 builds). 1.5.4 post-filters, misses from 32. Scoped semantic stays exact; test uses 4,096.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261022T012048Z-c88b51be7a8d7001","text":"pragma_hnsw_index_info approx_memory_usage is in-memory size, not disk: 21.0 MB (1.5.4) and 16.8 MB (2.0.0) for a 1,500-row index in a 9.2 MB file. Do not add it to a live-size or reclaimable estimate as disk bytes (measured 2026-10-21).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"7fc2e140e94a7ab1","sum":"HNSW pragma count 280901 vs 133793 rows, 39 GiB file, 1.5.4 and 2.0.0. Not proven deleted; hnsw_compact_index left them. LIMIT 100 returns 40-65. DROP+CREATE+CHECKPOINT (21s) makes count=rows and 100/100. count vs count(*) misses a folded index; own-vector lookup can. 2026-10-21.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261022T015815Z-5b6391ace5ed2f9b","text":"pragma_hnsw_index_info count includes deleted rows: the live 39 GiB warehouse reads 280,901 vs 133,793 rows while healthy (1.5.4 and 2.0.0). Count vs count(*) cannot detect a folded index there; an HNSW lookup of a known row by its own vector can. Measured 2026-10-21.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261022T023054Z-b85bc517446ce9b3","text":"Correction: the live HNSW index's 280,901 entries for 133,793 rows are not proven deleted rows; hnsw_compact_index left them. Unscoped LIMIT 100 returns 40-65 rows. DROP+CREATE+CHECKPOINT (21 s) gives count = rows and 100 of 100. Measured 2026-10-21 on 2.0.0.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
